# Copy to .env for local testing. review.py loads it automatically from the
# directory it lives in. Real environment variables always win over this file.
#
# .env is gitignored — never commit a real key.

# Required.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# GitHub auth — pick ONE of the two blocks below.

# (a) Easiest locally: a user token. `gh auth token` is used automatically if
#     neither this nor the App block is set, so you can often skip both.
#     Caveat: GitHub rejects APPROVE/REQUEST_CHANGES on your OWN PRs from a
#     user token, so test --post against someone else's PR, or use the App.
# GH_TOKEN=ghp_...

# (b) The GitHub App, as deployed. Reviews post as <slug>[bot], which is the
#     only identity that can review a PR the App itself authored. Requires the
#     openssl CLI. The PEM may use literal \n escapes on one line.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
# GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=7891011
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIE...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----

# Optional overrides (all have CLI equivalents — see --help).
# MODEL_LENS=z-ai/glm-5.2
# MODEL_VERDICT=deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro
# TARGET_REPOS=owner/repo,owner/other
# DRY_RUN=1
